From 5efa82236a0e92596961badad025b17b09d9e087 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Creitin Gameplays <clton999@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:08:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] mali: import Arm Mali Bifrost DDK r28p0-01eac0

Import the pristine Arm Bifrost/Valhall kernel driver r28p0-01eac0
(BX301A01B-SW-99002-r28p0-01eac0) as drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/, taken from
the batocera-linux/mali-bifrost mirror of the Arm community package.

This is the DDK version the shipping Moto E32 (hawaii, UMS9230/T606)
vendor mali_kbase.ko is built from (module version string
"r28p0-01eac0, UK version 11.29"), so its UK interface stays compatible
with the vendor libmali userspace.

The DDK interface headers (memory_group_manager.h and friends) are placed
in midgard/linux/ where the in-tree Kbuild include path (-I$(KBASE_PATH))
expects them, mirroring the layout Unisoc uses in their BSP forks.

Wired into drivers/gpu/Kconfig and drivers/gpu/Makefile
(obj-$(CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD)).  The platform glue follows in the next
commit; the driver is not yet buildable until the qogirl6 platform
adaptation lands.
